# MotherDuck Guides

Before querying MotherDuck, writing warehouse SQL, or changing dbt models that
land in `prod_*` / `dev_*` / `hub_*`, load the relevant Guides. Do not infer
join paths, grains, or metric definitions from table names alone.

Local Guides live under `transformation/guides/<prod_database>/<guide-slug>/guide.md`.
Always start with `transformation/guides/warehouse-overview/`.

When applying a prod Guide to `dev-cloud`, rewrite `prod_<name>` → `dev_<name>`
and prod schemas (`dbt_dmn`, …) → the developer schema `dbt_{user}`. Do not
change table names or business rules.

Suggest Guide updates; do not create or edit Guides unless the user asks.
